WEBVTT

00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:13,730
Would you explain your reservations and concerns with soft tissue radiation, please?

00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:18,370
To clarify soft tissue radiation on heart tumors as well.

00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:24,530
So by real reservation and concern with soft tissue radiation, quite honestly, my real reservation

00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:31,890
is when they do this, you know, blanket or radiation post breast cancer surgery.

00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:36,770
I really have a trouble with that. It just, to me, it doesn't make any sense whatsoever.

00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:44,290
We're okay. We're going to remove this, this, the, the tumor in the breast, and then we're going

00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:48,290
to do, we're going to radiate the whole breast. Come on. You know, if there's

00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:54,370
breast cancer cells still there, well, probably there probably is for sure, but you're going to

00:00:54,370 --> 00:01:02,690
cause just as many cancer cells damaging the tissue for the radiation. Besides the fact that if there's

00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:08,930
metastasis, it's, you know, the, the circulated tumor cells have taken off throughout the body

00:01:08,930 --> 00:01:14,210
already, and that's not going to help. But I am not, again, soft tissue radiation against a,

00:01:14,930 --> 00:01:20,130
you know, you've got a specific lymph node that you're hitting or a sarcoma or something like that

00:01:20,130 --> 00:01:26,130
that you're hitting. Certainly, radiations in the bone can kill or you can get very specific and

00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:38,370
targeted on a tuber itself. It's just this blanket radiation that I'm really against.

